{"metadata":{"title":"Performance","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI"],"title":"Related Documentation"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The binary-size budget, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" lifecycle guarantee, and the re-render characteristics of the default placeholders — what’s measured, what’s guaranteed, and why."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ScreenStates’ pitch is “small, dependency-free, drop into any screen.” This article covers the three ways that’s kept measurable rather than just assumed: a CI-enforced size budget, an audited concurrency guarantee, and a documented rendering characteristic."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The binary-size budget","anchor":"The-binary-size-budget"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"CI builds "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift build -c release"},{"type":"text","text":" on every push and sums the resulting "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".o"},{"type":"text","text":" sizes for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStates"},{"type":"text","text":" target, failing the build if that total exceeds the budget committed in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".github\/binary-size-budget.json"},{"type":"text","text":". There’s no single linked artifact to measure instead — the library product is “automatic,” and nothing in the package’s own build graph links it standalone — so the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".o"},{"type":"text","text":" total is the closest deterministic proxy available."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A legitimate feature addition that grows this total past the budget isn’t blocked forever: bump "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxBytes"},{"type":"text","text":" in that file as part of the same PR, the same way a dependency lockfile gets updated alongside the change that needed it. The job never bumps it on its own."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The Task lifecycle guarantee","anchor":"The-Task-lifecycle-guarantee"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refresh"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshCollection"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadWithRetry"},{"type":"text","text":" each store their running "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" in a private "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"currentTask"},{"type":"text","text":" property, read by "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/cancel()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"type":"text","text":". Every one of those "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":"s captures "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"self"},{"type":"text","text":" as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[weak self]"},{"type":"text","text":", not strongly — audited specifically to rule out a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"self -> currentTask -> closure -> self"},{"type":"text","text":" retain cycle keeping a store alive after its last external reference is dropped."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In practice, a completed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" releases its closure’s captures on return regardless of capture style, so this mostly matters for a still-"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"running"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" operation: without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[weak self]"},{"type":"text","text":", a store couldn’t become eligible for deallocation until that operation finished, even once every other reference to it was already gone. See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for the rest of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" lifecycle — cancellation, overlapping calls, and the automatic cancel-on-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"type":"text","text":" safety net this guarantee supports."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Re-render characteristics of the default placeholders","anchor":"Re-render-characteristics-of-the-default-placeholders"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/isRefreshing","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" only ever go active once "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refresh(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshCollection(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" have confirmed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"type":"text","text":" is already "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" — both fall back to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" otherwise, which never touch either property. That means "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" can never be observed alongside "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"type":"text","text":", so none of the three default placeholders can ever be on screen mid-refresh."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A parent view that reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.state"},{"type":"text","text":" (via "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":") and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" in the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" — the pattern "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" uses for a refresh toast — still has its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" re-evaluated whenever either changes, same as any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" property read in a SwiftUI "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":". This guarantee is about "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"which"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" placeholder that re-evaluation could ever affect, not about avoiding the re-evaluation itself: since a default placeholder is only ever on screen while "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" are both inactive, that re-evaluation never has a placeholder to needlessly re-render in the first place — only whatever renders the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" case could be affected."}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/performance"]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Performance","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore/cancel()":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatestore\/cancel()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cancel","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Cancels whatever ","type":"text"},{"code":"load","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"loadCollection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"refresh","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"refreshCollection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"loadWithRetry","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" call is currently in flight, if","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"any. ","type":"text"},{"code":"state","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (and ","type":"text"},{"code":"isRefreshing","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"refreshError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") are left exactly as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they were — cancelling never surfaces a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Ca